From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:04:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Build with modern compilers on 64-bit systems

- boolean: stay int-sized when stdbool.h is already included (SDL3)
- doomtype.h: stdint/stddef, alloca via __builtin_alloca; no <values.h>
- am_map.c: no implicit int
- m_misc.c: string defaults are pointers; keep them in intptr_t and store
  them through char** instead of truncating to int
- r_data.c: maptexture_t's obsolete columndirectory is 4 bytes in the WAD
- r_data.c, r_draw.c: align colormaps/translation tables via intptr_t
- z_zone.c: 8-byte block alignment; compare user tags via uintptr_t
- p_saveg.c: savegame indexes travel in pointer fields: cast via intptr_t
- d_net.c: offsetof instead of the null-pointer trick
- w_wad.c: no <malloc.h>/<alloca.h>
---
